<title>NETHERLANDS: Akzo plans French animal health R&amp;D centre.</title>
<headline>Akzo plans French animal health R&amp;D centre.</headline>
<dateline>ARNHEM, Netherlands 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch chemical group Akzo Nobel NV said its Intervet animal health unit planned to set up a new research and development centre at Angers in France which will employ about 110 people.</p>
<p>Akzo Nobel said the 30 million guilder investment was in line with Intervet's strategy of gradually increasing its presence in the global animal health market.</p>
<p>Intervet employs some 1,900 staff including 330 research and development staff who work at R&amp;D sites in the Netherlands, Denmark, Britain, the United States, Norway and Japan.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
